      "text": "Exercise 1’s supplied answer uses 3.34 × 10⁻¹⁰ cm, but the topic’s own 3.34 Å and Å-to-metre definition give 3.34 × 10⁻⁸ cm. It also divides one edge length even though the question asks for regions in a square face; using the printed spacing, the face count is (0.1/(3.34 × 10⁻⁸))², approximately 8.96 × 10¹². This checks the internal conversion and area count, not the physical lattice constant.",
